                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Representation used to evaluate coupling over this network's connectivity (``auto`` | ``dense`` | ``sparse``). ``auto`` lets the backend choose by connection density. This names whether to exploit edge sparsity, not a concrete data structure, so it is backend-independent; the delayed-vs-instantaneous graph kind is decided separately from the couplings' conduction delays." ;
