###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/newton_tol
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/newton_tol> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                   rdfs:label "newton_tol (slot)" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Absolute tolerance on the residual at which the Newton corrector has converged: the norm of the right-hand side f(x, p) at the corrected point must fall below it, in the units of f. BifurcationKit.jl applies it as that bound (NewtonPar tol). AUTO-07p tests the size of each Newton correction instead, relative to the size of the solution, so the AUTO-07p backends (auto-07p and pyrates-bifurcation) set both of its relative criteria to it, EPSL on the parameter and EPSU on the state, and only approximate the residual bound: a correction and the residual it removes differ by the conditioning of the Jacobian. Unset, each backend keeps its own default, BifurcationKit.jl 1e-12 on the residual and AUTO-07p 1e-7 on the correction. A branch's nested continuation that leaves it unset takes its parent's." ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "newton_tol" .


