###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/GraphRepresentation
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GraphRepresentation> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                  owl:unionOf ( <https://w3id.org/tvbo/GraphRepresentation#auto>
                                                                                <https://w3id.org/tvbo/GraphRepresentation#dense>
                                                                                <https://w3id.org/tvbo/GraphRepresentation#sparse>
                                                                              )
                                                                ] ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ;
                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                            rdfs:label "GraphRepresentation" ;
                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "How a Network's connectivity is represented when evaluating coupling. This is a backend-independent performance contract, not a numerical one: both representations compute the same coupling, but a sparse representation sums over the existing edges (cost scales with the number of edges) while a dense representation operates on the full adjacency (cost scales with nodes-squared). A backend maps the choice onto its own primitives (edge gather / segment-sum vs matrix product). Orthogonal to whether the coupling reads *delayed* states — that is decided per coupling by its conduction delay — so the two dimensions together yield the four backend graph kinds: dense/sparse × instantaneous/delayed." ;
                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> ;
                                            <https://w3id.org/linkml/permissible_values> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/GraphRepresentation#auto> ,
                                                                                         <https://w3id.org/tvbo/GraphRepresentation#dense> ,
                                                                                         <https://w3id.org/tvbo/GraphRepresentation#sparse> .


