###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/NodeReconciliation
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/NodeReconciliation> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                 owl:unionOf ( <https://w3id.org/tvbo/NodeReconciliation#by_label>
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/NodeReconciliation#none>
                                                                             )
                                                               ] ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ;
                                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                           rdfs:label "NodeReconciliation" ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strategy for aligning a sourced array's nodes to the consuming model network before use. Keyed alignment guards against a differing node count or ordering (e.g. a 998-parcel empirical FC against a 1000-parcel model, or a hemisphere-swapped connectome) silently misaligning the data." ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/common> ;
                                           <https://w3id.org/linkml/permissible_values> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/NodeReconciliation#by_label> ,
                                                                                        <https://w3id.org/tvbo/NodeReconciliation#none> .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/NodeSelection
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/NodeSelection> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/tvbo/applied> ;
                                                        owl:allValuesFrom xsd:boolean
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/tvbo/drop> ;
                                                        owl:allValuesFrom xsd:string
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/tvbo/keep> ;
                                                        owl:allValuesFrom xsd:string
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/tvbo/drop> ;
                                                        owl:minCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/tvbo/keep> ;
                                                        owl:minCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/tvbo/applied> ;
                                                        owl:minCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/tvbo/applied> ;
                                                        owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                      ] ;
                                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                      rdfs:label "NodeSelection" ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """The nodes of a network to keep or to drop, by label; exactly one of ``keep`` and ``drop`` is stated. A label is matched as written or through the aliases a ``by_label`` reconciliation uses (a node's ``alternateName`` and the atlas terminology). A selection is a set: the kept nodes stay in the order the network carries them, whatever order ``keep`` lists them in, and are renumbered from 0.
The selection is applied when the network is resolved, after its source has delivered nodes and arrays and before anything else reads them. Every stored layer, edge-parameter matrix and per-node array (``nodes/<name>``) is restricted to the kept nodes, an edge listed between two nodes goes with either of its nodes, and ``number_of_nodes`` is the kept count. Transforms, delays and couplings therefore see the selected network only: a normalisation by the largest weight is taken over the kept pairs. A layer or argument read through ``used:`` is read for the selected nodes: with ``reconcile: by_label`` it is aligned to them by name, without it the array has to come in the selected node count. A layer a ``producer:`` builds is not cut and has to come in the selected node count, and a per-node parameter read by ``source`` and ``measure`` from a network with more nodes is aligned to the kept nodes by label.
A warning names the network and both counts whenever a selection drops nodes from what the network carries; read back beside arrays that are already the selected ones, it drops none and gives none.
Refused, naming what is wrong: a label the network does not carry, ``keep`` beside ``drop``, a label listed twice, a selection that leaves no node, a node declared by label that the selection drops, and a network that carries a mesh or a route to another network, whose arrays the selection cannot restrict.""" ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/NodeSelection> ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .


