                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One cell of the figure. kind selects grammar (cartesian/heatmap) vs escape-hatch (image/custom); every kind shares the label, placeholder, legend and annotation machinery. Reuses label (human title)." ;
                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/figure> .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        owl:unionOf ( <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#cartesian>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#colorbar>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#custom>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#grid>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#heatmap>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#image>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#legend>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#line3d>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#network>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#surface>
                                                                      <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#volume>
                                                                    )
                                                      ] ;
                                  rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                  rdfs:label "PanelKind" ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What a panel draws. cartesian/heatmap are grammar-driven (mark + encoding); surface paints a layer on a mesh, volume projects one through a labelled volume and network draws one on a node-link graph; grid tiles a composite of sub-panels; colorbar/legend are shared keys in their own slot; image (external file) and custom (registered callable) are peer escape-hatch kinds. A new kind is added when its bsplot leaf exists." ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/figure> ;
                                  <https://w3id.org/linkml/permissible_values> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#cartesian> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#colorbar> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#custom> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#grid> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#heatmap> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#image> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#legend> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#line3d> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#network> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#surface> ,
                                                                               <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#volume> .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                           owl:unionOf ( <https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#auto>
                                                                         <https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#lax_map>
                                                                         <https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#pmap>
                                                                         <https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#vmap>
                                                                       )
                                                         ] ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ;
                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                     rdfs:label "ParallelMode" ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "How a trial / grid-point axis is realised at JAX codegen time. The choice trades peak memory against throughput: vmap batches in parallel (fast, n_trials × working-set memory), lax_map runs sequentially via ``jax.lax.map`` (memory bounded by one trial), pmap shards across devices, auto picks vmap when the estimated batched memory fits and lax_map otherwise." ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> ;
                                     <https://w3id.org/linkml/permissible_values> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#auto> ,
                                                                                  <https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#lax_map> ,
                                                                                  <https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#pmap> ,
                                                                                  <https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#vmap> .


