###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/SparseCoupling
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SparseCoupling> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                <https://w3id.org/tvbo/BackendCapability> ;
                                       rdfs:comment "Evaluate network coupling by summing over the existing edges only (cost scales with the number of edges) rather than over the full dense adjacency (cost scales with nodes-squared). Numerically identical to the dense evaluation; a pure performance optimisation for sparsely-connected networks."@en ;
                                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                       rdfs:label "Sparse (edge-list) coupling evaluation"@en ;
                                       <https://w3id.org/tvbo/boundConstraint> "edges << nodes^2  (connection density below the backend's sparse/dense crossover)" ;
                                       <https://w3id.org/tvbo/enabledByGraphParameter> "graph_representation" .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/SpikingSimulation
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SpikingSimulation> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                   <https://w3id.org/tvbo/BackendCapability> ;
                                          rdfs:comment "Integration of point-neuron populations with threshold-reset spiking and event-delivered synapses."@en ;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                          rdfs:label "Spiking (point-neuron) simulation"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/StaticDelayBuffer
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/StaticDelayBuffer> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                   <https://w3id.org/tvbo/BackendCapability> ;
                                          rdfs:comment "Fixed-length delay-history buffer (ceil(max_delay/dt) steps) whose size is set by an explicit max_delay bound and decoupled from the (possibly varying / traced) per-edge delays — the prerequisite for varying or differentiating delays under JIT. Delays exceeding max_delay are truncated (saturated at max_delay), so the bound must cover the slowest conduction speed explored."@en ;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                          rdfs:label "Static delay history buffer"@en ;
                                          <https://w3id.org/tvbo/boundConstraint> "max_delay >= max(tract_length) / min(conduction_speed)" ;
                                          <https://w3id.org/tvbo/enabledByGraphParameter> "max_delay" .


