###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/models/Antidots
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/models/Antidots> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                 <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Dynamics> ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> """Hamiltonian antidot lattice (periodic Sinai-like billiard) with smooth circular
repulsive potentials and perpendicular magnetic field. Models guiding center
dynamics and magnetotransport phenomena in mesoscopic systems. Smooth radial
repulsion implemented as a quartic polynomial potential inside radius (d0/2 + c)
matching the original implementation (Datseris 2019); outside region force is zero.""" ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/studies/Datseris2019> ;
