###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/networks/tpl-fsaverage_atlas-DesikanKilliany_desc-MEGAlpha_dscalar
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/networks/tpl-fsaverage_atlas-DesikanKilliany_desc-MEGAlpha_dscalar> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Network> ;
                                                                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> """Per-region MEG alpha-band amplitude values aligned with the 68 cortical parcels
of the Desikan-Killiany atlas. Sourced from
tvb-ontology-optim-workshop/notebooks/data/{lh,rh}_megalpha_parc.csv.

The measure exhibits the canonical cortical-hierarchy gradient:
  - unimodal sensory regions (pericalcarine, cuneus, lateraloccipital,
    transversetemporal) score high  (~0.40)
  - transmodal regions       (rostralanteriorcingulate, frontalpole,
    temporalpole, medialorbitofrontal) score low (~0.15)

Used as a per-region cortical-gradient signal in experiments that need
to ground a hierarchy (e.g. reservoir-computing frequency-gradient
targets, JR-MEG peak-frequency optimisation). The values are
dimensionless normalised amplitudes; downstream consumers rescale
to a task-appropriate range (e.g. omega in Hz).
""" ;
                                                                                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                                                                           rdfs:label "tpl-fsaverage_atlas-DesikanKilliany_desc-MEGAlpha_dscalar" ;
                                                                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Desikan-Killiany 68 cortical parcels with MEG alpha amplitudes per region" .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/networks/tpl-fsaverage_cohort-HCPYA_rec-avgMatrix_atlas-Lobar8_den-164k_desc-surf_relmat
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/networks/tpl-fsaverage_cohort-HCPYA_rec-avgMatrix_atlas-Lobar8_den-164k_desc-surf_relmat> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                                          <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Network> ;
                                                                                                                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The Lobar8 parcellation on both hemispheres of FreeSurfer's fsaverage, left then right, the right's triangles offset by the left's vertex count: TemplateFlow's `tpl-fsaverage_hemi-L|R_den-164k_pial.surf.gii`, each vertex taking the lobe of its Desikan-Killiany region in `tpl-fsaverage_hemi-L|R_den-164k_atlas-Desikan2006_seg-aparc_desc-curated_dseg.label.gii` by `DK_REGION_TO_LOBE` in `scripts/create_lobar8_surface.py` and indexing the 16 nodes of its parent network. Normals are each vertex's sum of its triangles' cross products, normalised. A medial-wall vertex takes the lobe of the nearest labelled vertex of its hemisphere, where the hemisphere surfaces keep it -1. The arrays are as commit 2766c501b wrote them." ;
                                                                                                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                                                                                                 rdfs:label "tpl-fsaverage_cohort-HCPYA_rec-avgMatrix_atlas-Lobar8_den-164k_desc-surf_relmat" ;
                                                                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Lobar8 surface (fsaverage 164k, 327684 vertices)" ;
                                                                                                                 <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/networks/tpl-fsaverage_cohort-HCPYA_rec-avgMatrix_atlas-Lobar8_den-164k_desc-surf_relmat/parameters/conduction_speed> .


