<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/members> rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                      rdfs:label "members (study)" ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The subject identifiers this cohort holds, without the ``sub-`` prefix, in the order a stacked read returns them. When the enclosing dataset lists its ``subjects``, every member must be one of them. A cohort states its members in exactly one way: typed here, read from ``members_file``, or admitted by ``rule``." ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/study> ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "members" .


<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/members_file> rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                           rdfs:label "members_file (study)" ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Path of a file that lists the members, read each time the cohort is used, so a list its producer keeps (the subjects a pipeline has finished) is never copied into the recipe. A ``.yaml`` or ``.json`` file holds what ``members`` would hold; a ``.tsv`` or ``.csv`` file is a participants table (the BIDS ``participants.tsv`` layout, tab- or comma-separated), read by its ``participant_id`` column, and a row with a value but no participant is an error; any other file holds one identifier per line, blank lines and lines starting with ``#`` skipped. Members come in the file's order and a ``sub-`` prefix is dropped. A relative path is read from the directory of the experiment or network file the dataset is part of, also when the dataset comes into that file by ``!include`` from another directory, and, when the file is not there, from the root of the study that file belongs to; a missing file is an error naming the places tried. Messages about a list read from a file give counts and positions, never an identifier." ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/study> ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "members_file" .


<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/metadata> rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                       rdfs:label "metadata (study)" ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Additional subject metadata as key-value pairs or path to a sidecar JSON file." ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/study> ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "metadata" .


<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/network> rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> ;
                                      rdfs:label "network (study)" ;
